#: ../../source/export.rst:185 4d0658ddb7a940868c93116adfc574b1
msgid ""
"The search mode is the one parameter that moves both time and memory by a"
" factor, and it moves them in opposite directions. ``fast`` wins on time "
"because OpenCV parallelises ``MODE_SGBM_3WAY`` over stripes while its "
"five-direction ``MODE_SGBM`` path barely scales past one core: on four "
"cores the two differ by 3.9x, and ``fast`` also finds 2.4 percentage "
"points more valid pixels for 5.1 MB more peak memory. The eight-direction"
" sweep is the expensive one — it keeps a full ``width x height x "
"numDisparities`` cost volume, which is 125 MB more and seven times the "
"time, for a disparity median that moves by half a pixel."
msgstr ""

